          %h3#Rheonomy Rheonomy
          %h4#idea_2 Idea
          %p
            In the formulation here the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+%28physics%29"} fields
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergravity"} supergravity
            are modeled by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+differential+forms"} super differential forms
            on a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supermanifold"} supermanifold
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tilde X
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supersymmetry"} supersymmetry
            manifest, i.e., serves to model geometry by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+supergeometry"} higher supergeometric
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+Cartan+geometry"} higher Cartan geometry
          %p
            But the actual fields of supergravity are supposed to be fields on actual
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetime"} spacetime
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            (an ordinary
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ↪
                    %mover
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \hookrightarrow \tilde X
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+differential+forms"} super differential forms
            used on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tilde X
            are uniquely determined by their restriction to ordinary
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+forms"} differential forms
            on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %em rheonomy
            (
            %a{:href => "#CastellaniDAuriaFre"}> Castellani-D’Auria-Fré 91, vol 2, section III.3.3
            ), alluding to the idea that the constraints allow the field data to “flow” from spacetime
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+spacetime"} super spacetime
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tilde X
          %p
            The idea here is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/analogy"} analogous
            (
            %a{:href => "#CastellaniDAuriaFre"}> Castellani-D’Auria-Fré 91, vol 2, p. 660
            ,
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#FreGrassi08"} Fré-Grassi 08, p. 4
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cauchy-Riemann+equations"} Cauchy-Riemann equations
            impose the constraint for a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function"} function
            on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+plane"} complex plane
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℂ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{C}
            to be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holomorphic+function"} holomorphic function
            and hence to be already fixed by its values on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+line"} real line
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi ℂ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R} \hookrightarrow \mathbb{C}
          %p
            In (
            %a{:href => "#CastellaniDAuriaFre"}> Castellani-D’Auria-Fré, vol 2, section III.3.3
            ) this idea is formalized by the constraint that for the given super-
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi L
                    %mn ∞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_\infty
            \-algebra connection as above, those components of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/curvature"} curvature
            forms which carry fermionic indices must be
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+combinations"} linear combinations
            of the components carrying no fermionic indices. (See also at
            = succeed ".)" do
              %em
                %a{:href => "infinity-Lie+algebroid-valued+differential+form#InfGaugeTrafo"} L-∞ algebra valued differential forms – integration of transformation
          %p
            This rheonomy constraint is equivalent to what elsewhere is called “superspace constraints”, see (
            %a{:href => "#AFFFTT98"}> AFFFTT 98, below (3.12)
            ).
          %p
            See also at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rheonomy+modality"} rheonomy modality
