              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0501007"}> arXiv:hep-th/0501007
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/j.physletb.2005.03.045"} doi:10.1016/j.physletb.2005.03.045
          %p
            Discussion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauged+supergravity"} gauged supergravity
            in this way:
          %ul
            %li#Fre05
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pietro+Fr%C3%A9"}> Pietro Fré
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em M-theory FDA, Twisted Tori and Chevalley Cohomology
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0510068"} arXiv:hep-th/0510068
          %p Independent dicussion of rheonomy in the guise of “superspace constraints”:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Warren+Siegel"}> Warren Siegel
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/S.+James+Gates+Jr."} S. James Gates Jr.
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Superfield supergravity
                %strong 147
                1–2 (1979) 77-104 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0550-3213(79)90416-4"}> doi:10.1016/0550-3213(79)90416-4
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/S.+James+Gates+Jr."}> S. James Gates Jr.
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kellogg+S.+Stelle"} Kellogg S. Stelle
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+C.+West"} Peter C. West
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Algebraic origins of superspace constraints in supergravity
                %strong 169
                3–4 (1980) 347-364 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0550-3213(80)90037-1"}> doi:10.1016/0550-3213(80)90037-1
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/S.+James+Gates+Jr."}> S. James Gates Jr.
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    On-shell and conformal
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi N
                          %mo =
                          %mn 4
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N=4
                    supergravity in superspace
                %strong 213
                3 (1983) 409-444 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0550-3213(83)90229-8"}> doi:10.1016/0550-3213(83)90229-8
                \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            The interpretation of the D’Auria-Fré-formulation as identifying supergravity fields as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-Lie+algebra+valued+differential+forms"} ∞-Lie algebra valued differential forms
            is in
          %ul
            %li#SSS
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hisham+Sati"}> Hisham Sati
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs Schreiber
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jim+Stasheff"} Jim Stasheff
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/L-%E2%88%9E+algebra+connections"} L-∞ algebra connections
              in
              = succeed "," do
                %em Quantum Field Theory
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://www.springerlink.com/content/p421153213548t31/"} publisher link
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0801.3480"} arXiv:0801.3480
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+integration"} Lie integration
            of that to genuine
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+%E2%88%9E-connections"} principal ∞-connections
            is in
          %ul
            %li#FiorenzaSchreiberStasheff10
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Domenico+Fiorenza"}> Domenico Fiorenza
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs Schreiber
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jim+Stasheff"} Jim Stasheff
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/Cech+cocycles+for+differential+characteristic+classes"} Čech cocycles for differential characteristic classes
              %strong 16
              1 (2012) &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1011.4735"}> arXiv:1011.4735
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+L-%E2%88%9E+algebras"} super L-∞ algebras
            that govern the construction are interpreted in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+gauge+theory"} higher gauge theory
            of an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/%E2%88%9E-Wess-Zumino-Witten+theory"} ∞-Wess-Zumino-Witten theory
            description of the
            = succeed "-type" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Green-Schwarz+sigma-model"} Green-Schwarz sigma-model
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/branes"} branes
            in
          %ul
            %li#FSS
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Domenico+Fiorenza"}> Domenico Fiorenza
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hisham+Sati"} Hisham Sati
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs Schreiber
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/The+brane+bouquet"} Super Lie n-algebra extensions, higher WZW models and super p-branes with tensor multiplet fields
              2013 (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1308.5264"}> arXiv:1308.5264
              )
          %p
            Apart from that the first vague mention of the observation that the “FDA”-formalism for supergravity is about higher categorical Lie algebras (as far as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} I
            am aware, would be grateful for further references) is page 2 of
          %ul
            %li#FreGrassi08
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pietro+Fr%C3%A9"}> Pietro Fré
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pietro+Antonio+Grassi"} Pietro Antonio Grassi
              %em Free differential algebras, rheonomy and pure spinors
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0801.3076"}> arXiv:0801.3076
              )
          %p
            An attempt at a comprehensive discussion of the formalism in the context of
            = succeed "-theory" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesive+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} cohesive (∞,1)-topos
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+super+%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} smooth super ∞-groupoid
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"}> Urs Schreiber
              ,
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/differential+cohomology+in+a+cohesive+topos"} differential cohomology in a cohesive topos
          %p To compare D’Auria-Fre with our language here, notice the following points in their book
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                The statement that a supergravity field is a morphisms
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mo :
                      %mi T
                      %mi X
                      %mo →
                      %mi inn
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi 𝔤
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi : T X \to inn(\mathfrak{g})
                or dually a morphism
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi Ω
                        %mo •
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ←
                      %mi W
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi 𝔤
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo :
                      %mi ϕ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega^\bullet(X) \leftarrow W(\mathfrak{g}) : \phi
                out of the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Weil+algebra"} Weil algebra
                of the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergravity+Lie+3-algebra"} supergravity Lie 3-algebra
                or similar is implicit in
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi I
                      %mn .3
                      %mn .122
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (I.3.122)
                (but it is evident, comparing with the formulas at
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Weil+algebra"} Weil algebra
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ϕ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi
                here a “soft form”.
            %li
              %p
                What we identify as gauge transformations and shifts by the characterization of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/curvature"} curvature
                forms on the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cylinder+object"} cylinder object
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                      %mo ×
                      %msup
                        %mi Δ
                        %mrow
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                          %mi p
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \times \Delta^{1|p}
                is their equation (I.3.36).
          %p Some more references:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pietro+Fr%C3%A9"}> Pietro Fré
                ,
                %em M-theory FDA, twisted tori and Chevalley cohomology
                (
                %a{:href => "http://www.arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0510068"}> arXiv
                )
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pietro+Fr%C3%A9"}> Pietro Fré
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pietro+Antonio+Grassi"} Pietro Antonio Grassi
                %em Pure spinors, free differential algebras, and the supermembrane
                (
                %a{:href => "http://www.arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0606171"}> arXiv:0606171
                )
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pietro+Fr%C3%A9"}> Pietro Fré
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pietro+Grassi"} Pietro Grassi
                %em Free differential algebras, rheonomy, and pure spinors
                (
                %a{:href => "http://www.arxiv.org/abs/0801.3076"}> arXiv:0801.3076
                )
          %p
            Discussion in this formalism of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Green-Schwarz+action+functional"} Green-Schwarz action functional
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M2-brane"} M2-brane
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sigma-model"} sigma-model
            with a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/target+space"} target space
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/11-dimensional+supergravity"} 11-dimensional supergravity
            background is in
          %ul
            %li#AFFFTT98
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gianguido+Dall%27Agata"}> Gianguido Dall'Agata
                , Davide Fabbri, Christophe Fraser,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pietro+Fr%C3%A9"} Pietro Fré
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    The
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi Osp
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn 8
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                          %mn 4
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Osp(8|4)
                    singleton action from the supermembrane
                %strong 542
                (1999) 157-194 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9807115"}> arXiv:hep-th/9807115
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li#FreGrassi07
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pietro+Fr%C3%A9"}> Pietro Fré
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pietro+Antonio+Grassi"} Pietro Antonio Grassi
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Pure Spinors, Free Differential Algebras, and the Supermembrane
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0606171"} arXiv:hep-th/0606171
          %p
            Relation to
            = succeed "-formalism:" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pure+spinor"} pure spinor
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pietro+Antonio+Grassi"}> Pietro Antonio Grassi
              ,
              %em
                Remarks on the Integral Form of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi D
                      %mo =
                      %mn 11
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D=11
                Supergravity
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2304.01743"}> arXiv:2304.01743
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p See also:
          %ul
            %li
              S. Salgado,
              %em Non-linear realizations and invariant action principles in higher gauge theory
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2312.08285"}> arXiv:2312.08285
              \&amp;rbrack;
        .revisedby
